The market is expected to remain cautious amid a bearish technical structure, elevated US bond yields and high oil prices, as investors also await the RBI's policy meeting next week. A decisive break below the Nifty 50's 22,550–22,500 support zone could trigger further selling, with a decline towards the April swing low near 22,200 not ruled out. On the upside, 22,800 remains the immediate hurdle, followed by 23,000. Meanwhile, Bank Nifty needs to defend the 54,000 level to sustain the possibility of a further upmove towards 55,000. A break below 54,000, however, could drag the index towards the 53,800–53,700 zone, according to experts.
On September 30, the Nifty 50 slipped 96 points, or 0.42 percent, to 22,620, while the Bank Nifty rallied 373 points, or 0.69 percent, to 54,633. Market breadth was largely neutral, with 1,629 stocks advancing compared with 1,619 stocks declining on the NSE.
 Sudeep Shah, Vice President - Technical and Derivatives Research at SBI Securities 
Nifty extended its corrective phase during the current week, continuing to exhibit a pattern of lower tops and lower bottoms on the daily chart. Since registering its recent peak of 24,774, the index has declined by more than 2,200 points within just 41 trading sessions, reflecting sustained weakness in the broader trend.
That said, selling pressure has eased over the last two trading sessions, with the index finding support near its 200-week SMA, a key long-term technical level. Momentum indicators continue to remain weak, as the daily RSI is positioned in the super bearish zone in line with RSI range shift rules. Additionally, the MACD histogram has remained below the zero line for the past 33 trading sessions, highlighting persistent negative momentum.
Going forward, the 22,550-22,500 zone will serve as an immediate support area. A decisive breach below 22,500 could accelerate the decline towards 22,200, where the previous swing low is positioned.
On the upside, the 22,850-22,900 zone is likely to act as a significant resistance, and the index needs to sustain above this band to indicate any improvement in sentiment.
 Strategy : Buy Nifty Futures above 22,750 with stop-loss of 22,600 and target of 23,050.
 Vatsal Bhuva, Technical Analyst at LKP Securities 
Nifty sentiment remains under pressure amid Brent crude around $100 a barrel, elevated US 10-year Treasury yields, and domestic factors such as the drought announcement in Maharashtra. The decisive breakdown below 23,000 indicates continued dominance of bears, supporting a sell-on-rise strategy.
Nifty formed a bearish candlestick on Wednesday, while RSI witnessed a bearish crossover. A hidden bearish divergence on the hourly chart also signals continuation of the downtrend. The immediate support zone is placed at 22,550–22,600, near the weekly 200-SMA, while 22,800 acts as resistance.
 Strategy : Conditional Sell Nifty October Futures below 22,650 with stop-loss of 22,800 and target of 22,400.
 Vaishali Patel, Deputy Manager - Research-Technical Department at Jainam 
